Leetcode:
29. Divide Two Integers

class Solution {
public:
    int divide(int dividend, int divisor) {
        if(dividend == divisor) 
            return 1;

        bool sign = true;
        if (dividend > 0 && divisor < 0) sign = false;
        else if(dividend < 0 && divisor > 0) sign = false;

        long n = abs((long)dividend);
        long d = abs((long)divisor);

        long quotient = 0;

        while(n >= d) {
            int cnt = 0;
            while(n >= (d << (cnt+1))) {
                cnt += 1;
            }

            quotient += (1LL << cnt);
            n -= (d << cnt);
        }
        if (quotient == (1LL << 31) && sign) {
            return INT_MAX;
        }

        if (quotient == (1LL << 31) && !sign) {
            return INT_MIN;
        }
        return sign ? quotient : -quotient;
    }
};

TC: O(logN)^2
Outer loop: Worst case say n = INT_MAX and divisor = 1 it will loop for O(logN) times.
Coz in every iteration we subtract the largest possible shifted divisor (d * 2^cnt) from n.
This eliminates the highest set bit of the quotient in each pass.

Inner loop: in worst case it also takes O(logN) operations to find the correct bit.

Note: As we are bounded by 32-bit integers the max number of operations is practically 31 * 31 = 961 that is it operates in O(1) relative time to input size.

SC: O(1)